      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Migration default sets every existing post to raw_html cooking",
      "description": "The migration adds `cook_method` with `default: 1, null: false`. `Post.cook_methods` is `Enum.new(:regular, :raw_html)`, and Discourse's `Enum` is zero-indexed, so `:regular` is 0 and `:raw_html` is 1. The default therefore marks every post that existed before this migration, and any post created without an explicit cook method, as raw HTML. `Post#cook` then returns `raw` for them and skips the rendering pipeline. The default should be `0` (`:regular`).",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "db/migrate/20131219203905_add_cook_method_to_posts.rb:2"
    },
    {
      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Stray `if` after `end` in the best-posts template",
      "description": "The line `<%- end if %>` closes the `if @topic_view.posts.present?` block with a dangling modifier `if` that has no condition. Ruby will reject this as a syntax error, or misparse the following output lines as the condition. The `if` should be removed so the line reads `<%- end %>`.",
